WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.840
On Friday the 9th of April 2021, we received&nbsp;
the very sad news that His Royal Highness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:10.320
The Prince Philip, Duke of Edinburgh&nbsp;
had passed away at the age of 99.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.400
His contribution to our nation serving loyally at&nbsp;
the side of Her Majesty The Queen for more than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:23.520
70 years cannot be underestimated. In addition,&nbsp;
the young people in the District have benefited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:28.960
significantly from participating in the Duke of&nbsp;
Edinburgh's Awards Scheme for a number of years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.600
a scheme founded by him which has enabled&nbsp;
many young people to build the skills&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.080
confidence and resilience they have needed&nbsp;
in order to make the most of their lives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:45.040
Our thoughts are with Her Majesty The Queen&nbsp;
and The Royal Family who have lost a husband,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:51.120
father, grandfather and great-grandfather. I&nbsp;
have written to The Queen's Private Secretary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:56.400
to express condolences to her and the Royal&nbsp;
Family on behalf of Rochford District Council.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:03.200
The Council's flag has also been lowered to&nbsp;
half mast as a sign of respect. I've also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:08.240
cancelled any civic engagements of a social&nbsp;
or fundraising nature during this sad time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:15.360
A period of national mourning has begun and will&nbsp;
continue until the funeral takes place at 3pm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:22.000
on Saturday, the 17th of April. The Royal Family&nbsp;
has asked that during this difficult time floral&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.120
tribute should not be left at Royal Residences&nbsp;
and that we should all continue to follow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:33.360
public health guidance, particularly on avoiding&nbsp;
meeting in large groups and or minimising travel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.920
I would therefore urge residents&nbsp;
not to travel to London&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:42.960
or any of the Royal Residences, in order to&nbsp;
respect the wishes of the Royal Household.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:48.080
I know that many residents will be feeling&nbsp;
saddened and will want to commemorate this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:53.360
sad loss; however, can I please urge you&nbsp;
to follow the wishes of the Royal Family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:58.560
relating to floral tributes and to refrain from&nbsp;
leaving floral tributes within our District.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:04.400
The website the Royal Household has suggested&nbsp;
that residents may wish to consider instead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:10.080
making a donation to a charity of their choice&nbsp;
or to one of the Duke of Edinburgh's patronages.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:16.720
Due to the need to maintain prevailing public&nbsp;
health coronavirus restrictions and government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:22.640
has stipulated there will be no physical Book of&nbsp;
Condolence at the Council. The Royal Household has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:28.320
set up an online book of condolence which&nbsp;
can be found at www.royal.uk/condolence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.160
so that residents can leave their personal&nbsp;
messages during this national time of mourning.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:40.720
Formal arrangements are currently being&nbsp;
finalised so we can all commemorate the life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:46.240
of His Royal Highness The Prince Philip, Duke&nbsp;
of Edinburgh. Please go to the Royal Household&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:56.880
website at www.royal.uk/home-royal-family if&nbsp;
you would like more information. In the meantime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:01.840
Rochford District Council will be holding a&nbsp;
two-minute silence in honour of His Royal Highness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:06.000
The Prince Philip, Duke of Edinburgh which&nbsp;
will be streaming on our YouTube channel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:14.080
on Friday the 16th of April at 9 30 a.m so that&nbsp;
residents can watch live. The link can be found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:22.840
on the front page of the council's website&nbsp;
www.youtube.com/user/rochfordcouncil

